Subject: EDHREC: read the current average-deck and commander page shapes

json.edhrec.com/pages/average-decks/<slug>.json now sends "deck" as an
object: {"commander": [name], "commander_v2": [[name, 1]],
"cards": {"Artifact": [[name, qty], ...], "Land": [...], ...}}. Mystic Forge
1.3.2 iterates it as a list of lines, so edhrec_average_deck printed the three
key names and "Total: 3 cards". The page also no longer has avg_price.
Checked live on 2026-10-04 for Aesi, Tyrant of Gyre Strait; Atraxa,
Praetors' Voice; and Kenrith, the Returned King: same shape each time,
1 commander + 99 cards.

The commander page (pages/commanders/<slug>.json) no longer has
num_decks_avg or avg_price either, so edhrec_commander printed
"Based on ? decks | Avg price: $?". The deck count is now at
container.json_dict.card.num_decks (17254 for Aesi on 2026-10-04).

This patch prints the average deck by card type with quantities and a real
total, keeps the old list shape working, reads the deck count from the card
entry, and leaves out the price line when EDHREC sends no price.
Tests: tests/test_edhrec_current_shape.py.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 (main, 2026-10-04) has no fix,
and no open pull request touches this code. Drop this patch when it does.

diff --git a/server.py b/server.py
index 4dafd14..ffd28ce 100644
--- a/server.py
+++ b/server.py
@@ -1159,7 +1159,14 @@ async def edhrec_commander(params: CommanderInput) -> str:
 
     parts: list[str] = []
     parts.append(f"# {data.get('header', params.name)}")
-    parts.append(f"Based on {data.get('num_decks_avg', '?')} decks | Avg price: ${data.get('avg_price', '?')}")
+    # EDHREC's commander pages no longer carry num_decks_avg or avg_price; the
+    # deck count now sits on the commander's own card entry.
+    card = ((data.get("container") or {}).get("json_dict") or {}).get("card") or {}
+    num_decks = data.get("num_decks_avg") or card.get("num_decks") or "?"
+    line = f"Based on {num_decks} decks"
+    if data.get("avg_price") is not None:
+        line += f" | Avg price: ${data['avg_price']}"
+    parts.append(line)
     parts.append("")
 
     types = ["creature", "instant", "sorcery", "artifact", "enchantment", "planeswalker", "land"]
@@ -1201,11 +1208,35 @@ async def edhrec_average_deck(params: CommanderInput) -> str:
 
     parts: list[str] = []
     parts.append(f"# {data.get('header', f'Average Deck for {params.name}')}")
-    parts.append(f"Avg price: ${data.get('avg_price', '?')}")
+    if data.get("avg_price") is not None:
+        parts.append(f"Avg price: ${data['avg_price']}")
     parts.append("")
 
     deck = data.get("deck", [])
-    if deck:
+    if isinstance(deck, dict):
+        # Current EDHREC shape: {"commander": [name, ...],
+        # "cards": {"Creature": [[name, qty], ...], ...}}.
+        total = 0
+        commanders = [c for c in deck.get("commander") or [] if isinstance(c, str)]
+        if commanders:
+            parts.append("## Commander")
+            for name in commanders:
+                parts.append(f"1 {name}")
+                total += 1
+            parts.append("")
+        for card_type, entries in (deck.get("cards") or {}).items():
+            lines = [(e[0], e[1]) for e in entries or []
+                     if isinstance(e, (list, tuple)) and len(e) == 2
+                     and isinstance(e[0], str) and isinstance(e[1], int)]
+            if not lines:
+                continue
+            parts.append(f"## {card_type}")
+            for name, qty in lines:
+                parts.append(f"{qty} {name}")
+                total += qty
+            parts.append("")
+        parts.append(f"Total: {total} cards")
+    elif deck:
         for line in deck:
             parts.append(line)
         parts.append("")
